7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
or hiking, or maybe you make some up just to go camping.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
I have found that there are two basic ingredients to trail mix.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
There are M&M's and disappointment.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Do you know exactly what I'm talking about?

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Hey, this is podcast number 245..

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Hey,

13
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Hey,

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Welcome back to the Scoutmaster podcast.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
This is Clark Green.

16
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Let's take a look in the mailbag.

17
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
I'm Donald Fowler, and Don said it's been five months since I've become Scoutmaster.

18
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,000
I'm having a blast.

19
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Our patrol leaders council is taking on more responsibility each month.

20
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,000
My next challenge, of course, is getting the adult leaders to stay away from the Scouts during campouts.

21
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Well, Don, first, I am really happy to hear you're having a blast.

22
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
It is the best job going, isn't it?

23
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Being a Scoutmaster. I love it.

24
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
And there are challenges, and that's a very common challenge.

25
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
If you get there, you're going to get those adults right on board

26
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
and things are going to keep getting better.

27
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
That's my prediction.

28
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,000
How about that?

29
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Don went on to say.

30
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:05,000
I recently heard about a troop with over 100 Scouts with some unusual practices.

31
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
They will not allow a Scout to advance more than one rank per year

32
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:15,000
because they feel that Scouts who reach Eagle any younger than age 17 aren't mature enough.

33
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,000
They look down on any Scout who earned Eagle at a younger age.

34
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
I did mention to them that this goes against the Guide to Advancement

35
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,000
And the answer I got back was: well, that's how we've always done things

36
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
And since we have the biggest troop in the area, it proves that we're right.

37
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Well, Don, of course it's pretty much a no-brainer, isn't it?

38
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The policies you described that this troop has adopted

39
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
are specifically prohibited in the Guide to Advancement.

40
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
It's right there in black and white.

41
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
It's not hard to figure that one out.

42
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
What I think is stunning is that people who are expected to model

43
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:57,000
the virtues of loyalty and obedience to young people

44
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
can decide that they're a rule to themselves.

45
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Beyond that, they're convinced that they follow a higher and better rule

46
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,000
than the rest of us poor brunited souls out here. you know,

47
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:15,000
I mean the hypocrisy in that would be comedic if it was not so tragic.

48
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,000
I will say what I have often said: there's one way to become an Eagle Scout,

49
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
and that's completing the requirements as written.

50
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
There's nothing about your age in those requirements is there?

51
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,000
If it was written, I could understand it, but it's not there.

52
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Adding to the requirements in the way that this troop has done

53
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:37,000
is just as misguided as detracting from the requirements.

54
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Unfortunately, though you know, this is not the first troop

55
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
I've ever heard of that does things this way.

56
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,000
I've known troops in my own council like this that have set up

57
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:51,000
their own higher standard of what an Eagle Scout ought to be,

58
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,000
and they are usually insufferably proud of themselves,

59
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
But, like the Emperor with no clothes,

60
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:02,000
they fail to understand that their naked disloyalty

61
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
and disobedience is plainly visible

62
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:08,000
and, honestly, I'm just plain embarrassed for them.

